# /Users/grayson is a git repo (origin: graysonpope007/CLEETUS).
# That means an unguarded `git add -A` here would stage your ENTIRE home
# directory — ~/.ssh private keys, ~/.claude.json, ~/.config, shell history.
#
# So: ignore everything by default, then allowlist only the paths this repo
# tracks. Adding a new project? Add a matching `!` pair below.
#
# Note: this does not untrack anything already tracked; edits and deletions to
# tracked files still show up in `git status` and still commit normally. The
# merged `.claude/` and `.agent/` trees are tracked but deliberately NOT
# allowlisted — that keeps the rest of your live ~/.claude (sessions, history,
# projects, todos) invisible to git.

# 1. Deny everything.
/*

# 2. Allowlist the tracked projects. Each needs the dir unignored AND a
#    recursive re-ignore/unignore pair, because git will not descend into an
#    excluded directory to find negations inside it.
!/README.md
!/.gitignore

!/calm-therapy-template/
!/cleetus/
!/gp-productions-booking/

# cleetusd — the Cleetus that has the disk. It had never been tracked ANYWHERE,
# which for the process holding run_shell and the tool loop is a bad place to
# leave it. Its secrets are not in the tree: config.mjs reads them out of
# Documents/Claude/Projects/Cleetus V2/cleetus.env, which this repo never sees.
!/cleetusd/

# 3. Junk that should never be committed even inside an allowlisted project.
.DS_Store
*.swp
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.*
credentials.json
token.json
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# 4. The Obsidian vault is its own git repo — tracked separately, not a submodule.
vault/
